{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"kinglike-absurd-thrip","creation_channel":"python","description":"Discovered from 8408-54bb (Gerrit change 2071 PS2 LLM-Review advisory, correctness, src/rebar/_errors.py:108).\n\nerror_code_for step 4 classifies EVERY ConfigError subclass as `config_unreadable` by isinstance, including InsecureUrlError (src/rebar/_config_schema.py) — which was explicitly designed to let a caller tell a deliberate cleartext-URL security-policy rejection apart from a malformed-config parse fault (bug bdb8). An MCP client branching on `config_unreadable` would mis-prompt the operator to 'fix an unreadable config' when the config parsed fine and was rejected by policy.\n\nProposed: classify InsecureUrlError before the ConfigError arm (a distinct code, e.g. `config_insecure_url`, added to KNOWN_ERROR_CODES), or exclude the subclass from step 4 and let it fall through to a deliberate code. Keep parity in docs/mcp-reference.md via scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py (the doc is generated). This is a behavioral classification choice — confirm the desired code name before implementing.","id":"7d6a-16d2-ef8a-4b47","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"error_code_for: split InsecureUrlError out of config_unreadable"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787382726595054001,"uuid":"856cbfbf-599b-4fe2-8d5f-0575e848915a"}